WEBVTT

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.590
I got it!

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.650
This is a big one!

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.830
Congratulations!

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.470
Hey, Ippo,

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:19.770
leave the boat to me and the boss and focus on your boxing already.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.530
I can't do that!

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:24.160
Yeah, but you're fighting him soon, right?

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.160
The world champion!

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.320
Ippo-kun!

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.410
You've got a world title match coming up?

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.420
When is it?

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.460
The time's finally come!

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.840
Um, no, it's not like that!

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.580
Yes, I'm going to be fighting against the world champion,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.250
but it's just sparring, so...

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.540
Oh, so it's not a world title match.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.890
Even so, that's still impressive.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.650
It'll be a good experience for you.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:47.930
Good luck, Ippo-kun!

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.400
Right!

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.760
I'll do my best!

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.690
So, how strong is this Ricardo guy?

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.430
I can't even imagine it.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.440
He's fought 62 matches and is undefeated!

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.700
That's unbelievable!

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.250
Just the fact that he has fought in 62 matches already is hard enough,

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.950
but to not lose at all-

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.620
All right, all right, I get it.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.360
I get that the champion is badass.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.070
But if you think about it,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.160
him winning 62 times

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.030
means he's got about 5 times as many wins compared to your 13.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.880
So, it's not like he's 20 or 30 times stronger.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.770
It'd be easier if you thought of it as fighting against five of yourself.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.130
I never thought of it like that.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:30.110
So, think of it as fighting against five of myself.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.810
I-If we all punched at once, I could only hit one of them.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.980
You've got a better imagination than I thought.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.420
The fact that you could hit one of the five is what's important.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.590
In other words, if he hits you five times, then you might be able to hit him once.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.640
It's not that simple!

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.650
This is a historic super champ we're talking about!

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.990
He'll probably just play around with me!

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.420
I don't think so!

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.620
You're still the Japanese Champion, right?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.830
Human stamina has a limit, no matter how hard a person trains himself!

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.280
Your punches push people over that limit!

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.970
If you can hit him,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.560
even if he's the world champion, he'll still fall!

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.370
The world champion...

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.860
would fall?

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.360
Show the strongest guy in the world

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.200
what you're made of.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.060
Yeah.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.790
At the very least, I'll fight him seriously.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.220
I want to see how strong I am right now.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.010
<i>He's so incredible... that it's a little scary,</i>

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.840
<i>but I may never get a chance like this again!</i>

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.980
<i>I'll go all out!</i>

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.000
T-There he is!

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.390
Get the camera ready!

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.850
Let's see if we can get a comment from him!

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.650
Among the entourage is his trainer and manager, Bill Stewart.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.020
He's a big-shot trainer who's trained seven world champions.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.110
And behind him...

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.670
The historic hero has finally arrived.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.390
The WBA World Featherweight Champion,

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.630
Ricardo Martinez.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.430
Hey, Ippo!

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:31.500
So, the time's finally come for you to fight the world champion, huh?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.320
It's not like it's a real fight.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.180
Nah,

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.190
the champion hasn't been in the country for long yet.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.070
You might be able to land one on him if he's still jet-lagged.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.630
Y-You think I can?

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.610
Dumbass!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.510
Have fun getting destroyed!

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.080
You look lost in thought.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:01.500
Don't tell me that you're thinking you might stand a chance.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.340
N-No, of course not.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.480
I understand your desire to test your strength,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:12.360
but you're up against a famous champion who's already considered legendary before his career has even ended.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.770
He's not someone that you could possibly have any hope against.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:20.770
If you can graze him with even one shot, you might get a reaction out of him.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.520
Do that much and you'll have my praise.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.720
Just grazing him...

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.090
It doesn't sound like much of an accomplishment, but...

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.910
the spar is for three rounds, right?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.180
If I throw 200 punches per round,

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:37.150
then in three rounds, I'd be throwing 600 punches.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.290
If I throw at least that many, I'm sure one will graze him!

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.200
All right, I'm going to graze him!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.880
<i>The best case scenario...</i>

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.300
<i>If the kid can land a proper punch,</i>

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.840
<i>even the champion wouldn't escape unscathed.</i>

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.870
<i>Forget getting a reaction from him,</i>

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.060
<i>there's a good chance he might fall.</i>

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.490
Coach Kamogawa, Ippo-kun...

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.930
The sparring with the Japanese rankers has already started.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.100
How is Ricardo Martinez?

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.470
Well, he's showing off superior techniques, but...

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.900
...to be honest, he's holding back.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.200
I came to gather some intel on him, but at this rate, I'll have nothing to report to Date.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.220
Coach Nakadai...

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.360
For now, just watch closely.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:23.960
Right!

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:27.550
<i>I really am getting nervous.</i>

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.550
<i>The world champion is in there.</i>

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.290
<i>The strongest man in the world.</i>

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.460
<i>It's really him!</i>

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.090
<i>The legendary world champion...</i>

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.440
<i>is right in front of me!</i>

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.690
The second spar is about to start.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.730
Yes. {jama: added}

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.640
P-Pleased to meet you!

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.250
I-I'll do my best!

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.360
The first one was like that too.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.700
At this rate, there's no way the champion will ever get in the mood.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.070
I don't blame them.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.770
He's more of a famous hero to them than an enemy.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.340
They probably feel like it's an honor to be able to stand in the same ring as him.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.840
<i>I know how they feel.</i>

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.860
He's in complete control.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:25.060
I'm hoping you'll be able to force the champion to take this seriously.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.690
I want to take something back to Date.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.090
<i>He's in the same weight class as me.</i>

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.800
<i>He's a little bit taller,</i>

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.470
<i>but our builds aren't that different.</i>

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:35.690
<i>He's only human.</i>

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:36.710
<i>Don't be intimidated.</i>

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.800
Thank you so much!

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.830
Next person, you're up!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.200
Right!

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.340
Pleased to meet you!

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:55.980
Kid...

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:57.400
He's wearing his fighting gear?

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.100
He's really ready to go.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.800
This guy's the Japanese Champion.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:04.100
It seems he pushed Eiji Date pretty hard.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:09.860
Based on the fact that he isn't wearing headgear, he probably wants to feel the full impact of your power.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.200
You can handle this however you want.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.660
Forcibly put him down, or run circles around him...

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.430
Just show him the difference between where he's at and the world champ.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.530
<i>This kind of excitement is bad for my heart at this age.</i>

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.880
<i>My boxer is facing down the world champion.</i>

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.010
<i>Even the smallest chance is enough to get me worked up.</i>

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.980
<i>Japan's hope against the world champion...</i>

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.890
<i>Even though it's just a spar, you could still sell tickets to something like this.</i>

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.130
<i>Seeing him up close like this...</i>

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.650
<i>He seems too big to be in the same weight class.</i>

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.720
<i>The pressure alone is enough to crush you.</i>

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.100
<i>Go for it, Kid!</i>

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.280
<i>Make an impression on the champion!</i>

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:07.720
<i>Before I get overwhelmed, I need to start my rhythm!</i>

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.290
<i>Go at full blast from the start!</i>

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.380
Makunouchi made the first move!

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.530
<i>I don't know how far I can take this,</i>

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.130
<i>but I'll go as far as I can!</i>

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.590
A left!

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:18.880
He's using the speed of his dash!

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.920
No, it was a feint!

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.010
He made a high feint but came in low! {jama: I hope solo can shorten this line somehow :P}

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.020
It's his specialty, the liver blow!

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:31.450
<i>He saw through it!</i>

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.010
<i>Regular feints won't work!</i>

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.050
<i>It wasn't a bad idea.</i>

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.650
<i>Use that speed to keep the champion off balance!</i>

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:39.940
<i>If vertical variations won't work, then horizontal...</i>

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.530
<i>I'll mix it up from the sides!</i>

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.200
He's started bobbing his head!

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.030
It's like he's fighting in a real match.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.410
<i>So he uses the Peek-a-Boo style, weaving his upper body and then stepping in?</i>

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.970
<i>He's similar to Mike Tyson,</i>

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.580
<i>and I'm sure he's powerful too.</i>

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.920
<i>He might end up being a thrilling partner to spar with.</i>

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.950
<i>If I keep punching, I know I'll connect sooner or later!</i>

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.340
<i>If I can connect,</i>

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:02.430
<i>I can get into my rhythm!</i>

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:10.820
<i>What was that?</i>

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.760
<i>Something nailed me in the middle of my one-two.</i>

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.030
<i>The champion hasn't changed his stance.</i>

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.540
<i>Was it a left or a right?</i>

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.780
<i>Which one was I hit with?</i>

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.760
<i>Either way, I have to try and hit him!</i>

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.030
<i>I have to start my rhythm!</i>

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:25.230
<i>Calm down...</i>

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.030
<i>Calm down...</i>

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.540
<i>Just step in under his left like you always do, {TLC- Step in after he throws his left?}</i>

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.820
<i>and press into his chest!</i>

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.290
He was hit again!

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.630
He's landing lefts so easily.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.970
<i>It's like his glove got huge all of a sudden!</i>

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.300
<i>I can't grasp the timing to step in!</i>

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:44.700
How can it be so easy for him?

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.750
Is there some trick to it?

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.430
It's no trick.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.150
There's no gimmick or secret behind it at all.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:50.810
Nothing?

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:56.310
With human reflexes, dodging a punch after you see it coming is near impossible.

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:00.610
What you gain through experience and training is the ability...

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:04.950
to predict when the punch comes based on the movement of your opponent's shoulder or elbow.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.320
However,

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:09.200
the champion's punch flew along the most direct path possible,

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.450
without moving his shoulder and elbow at all.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:11.550
In other words,

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.460
without a signaling motion, it can't be predicted.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:16.790
There's no trick,

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.520
it's more like a left rooted in the most basic of fundamentals.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.940
It's something that's only possible by checking your form in a mirror tens of thousands of times, as you practice.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.720
So even his regular left is top-grade material.

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.990
H-Hey, is it getting to him?

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:33.520
But Makunouchi's made it this far as a boxer because of his toughness,

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.200
and the champion hasn't used anything but a left so far!

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.070
<i>That left is more effective than you'd think.</i>

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.030
<i>Mexican punches are thrown in a way where they reach farther than you'd think and...</i>

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.710
<i>since you've already extended yourself into a position where you expect to dodge it,</i>

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:48.620
<i>you can't brace yourself to absorb the shock.</i>

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>If you don't do something soon, Makunouchi-kun...</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.620
<i>you're going to be beaten left-handedly.</i>

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.450
I can't believe it.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.130
Ippo-kun's being beaten with just a left.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.270
<i>These lefts really cut to the bone.</i>

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:03.050
<i>If I keep getting hit like this, I'll be knocked down!</i>

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.630
<i>I'm trying everything I can think of...</i>

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.390
<i>but I can't land anything!</i>

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.390
<i>Not even one!</i>

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:13.150
<i>The champion's only using his left,</i>

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.390
<i>but I can't do a thing.</i>

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.270
<i>The difference is this big?</i>

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.890
<i>It's this great?</i>

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.750
It's affecting his legs.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:34.870
This is bad.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:38.120
He really is going to lose to someone using just a left.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:39.970
<i>This is pathetic...</i>

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.110
<i>So pathetic!</i>

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.190
<i>But if I can just...</i>

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:44.370
<i>just land one hit...</i>

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.380
<i>A single hit to get a reaction out of him!</i>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:48.630
<i>He can do it.</i>

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.600
<i>The kid has a weapon...</i>

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.890
<i>that the champion will have to respond to!</i>

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:02.020
<i>I shouldn't try to evade his punches anymore.</i>

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.400
<i>There's no way I can dodge his left!</i>

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:12.660
<i>I have to block each one carefully.</i>

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.110
He's blocking them and slowly closing in.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:21.380
<i>Just a little further...</i>

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:26.800
He's pressed all the way in!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.050
He was waiting to get into his best range!

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.050
<i>Now!</i>

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:41.810
There it is!

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.820
The Dempsey Roll!

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.150
That's it!

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:48.890
There are few people in the world that can use the Dempsey Roll!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:52.240
If it's a punch he's never encountered before, even the champion won't know how to react!

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.740
Even if it's the champion, if it lands...

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.250
<i>If I keep going at this rate, I should be able to land at least one.</i>

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.330
Go, Kid!

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:22.770
I-Impossible...

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:26.010
He was able to follow the horizontal movement and still land his left!?

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:30.780
He could still see him even though he was weaving so fast!?

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:33.240
I-It's incredible.

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:35.740
There are no words for it.

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:42.650
C-Champion,

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.540
the spar isn't over yet!

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.290
Gentlemen...

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:50.550
Ricardo doesn't intend to crush the Japanese Champion's pride.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:53.330
He simply came here today to warm up his left,

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:57.050
and, with that done, there's no need to continue.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:00.060
Kid, get your clothes on, we're heading back.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.560
Kid...

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:09.940
What are you doing!? It's over, Kid!

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.280
We're going home!

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:14.410
Coach?

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.700
<i>He was unconscious?</i>

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.450
<i>And the champion realized that...</i>

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:24.710
<i>Not knocking the kid down in front of this huge crowd must've been an act of mercy.</i>

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:27.610
Give your thanks to the champion!

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.450
I see...

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.630
It's over then...

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:36.840
Thank you very much!

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:43.280
This is huge news!

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.990
The world champion reigns supreme!

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:47.690
And dominates the Japanese Champion with just his left!

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:51.920
Sounds like you'll be getting a lot of coverage in the sports pages of tomorrow's papers.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:52.810
Right...

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:53.650
It's fine.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.910
I didn't expect you to do well at your current level anyway.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.950
If you were able to grasp the difference of the world level, then it was worth it.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:03.890
The world level...

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:05.570
You understand?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.280
To be honest...

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:09.460
I don't.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:11.980
I wasn't able to do anything at all,

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.290
so it doesn't feel real.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.240
He was too strong,

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:17.490
and there was such a big difference.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.470
I couldn't do anything.

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:29.980
To think that there'd be someone capable of using the Dempsey Roll in the Pacific Region.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.670
I'll be honest, I was surprised.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:34.690
He seemed to have plenty of destructive power as well.

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:37.490
Did it worry you for a moment?

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:41.380
A stupid question, I guess...

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:45.250
No matter who your opponent is or what they do, there's no way it'd surprise you.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:48.780
You'll have to remind Eiji Date of that again as well,

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:51.790
how high the world summit is.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.710
Hold on, Ippo! What happened to your face!?

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.020
Take a look in the mirror! It's a mess.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:04.400
T-This is terrible!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:07.520
And it was only one round and just his left too...

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.070
This is the world's strongest left.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:15.020
<i>Can Date-san win?</i>

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:18.780
<i>I don't think I can ever see that champion losing.</i>

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.280
<i>I can't imagine it.</i>

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.140
There it is, splashed all over the page!

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:28.040
"Shut out with just a left."

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.450
I don't care how strong your opponent is, at least make 'em use both arms.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:33.190
You're the shame of Japan!

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:36.780
Think about the pressure you've put on him now!

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.170
I-I'm sorry...

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.160
If you're gonna apologize, apologize to the old man.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.890
Go give him your regards.

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:44.720
Yeah,

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:47.410
but what kind of face am I supposed to put on for him?

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:48.780
That busted up one!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.190
This is depressing...

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.510
Just by looking at my face,

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.580
he can probably see the power of the champion's punches.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:04.830
What will I say?

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.830
What do I do?

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:14.400
<i>Is it a spar?</i>

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.220
Date-san!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.430
He looks cool with a full beard grown out all the way!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:23.440
Who's his sparring partner?

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.180
Most people wouldn't be able to keep-

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.310
Miyata-kun!?

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:33.310
Yeah, the Oriental Pacific Region Champion would definitely make a suitable partner!

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:37.820
<i>Miyata-kun's left flies from his shoulder to its target along the quickest path possible too.</i>

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:40.550
<i>It's a lot like the champion's.</i>

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.070
<i>He dodged that left!</i>

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.890
<i>And then he fires right back!</i>

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:50.540
<i>He wouldn't be able to do that if he couldn't follow the punches.</i>

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.510
<i>Amazing...</i>

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:56.550
<i>Takamura-san might have sent me here just to watch this amazing spar.</i>

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.590
<i>Miyata-kun is really serious.</i>

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:03.800
<i>This might as well be a match to determine the strongest featherweight in the nation!</i>

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.630
<i>He's not taking any lefts.</i>

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:10.100
<i>At this rate, he might be able to dodge the champion's left too!</i>

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.880
<i>I guess he's a level above me when it comes to trading lefts.</i>

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.950
<i>No time to aim a counter either!</i>

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:20.480
<i>In that case...</i>

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.030
<i>He went to fight it out!</i>

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:28.570
<i>What an incredible high-speed battle.</i>

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:31.230
<i>But Miyata-kun is quicker,</i>

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.870
<i>so the faster they go...</i>

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.920
Thank you, Pacific Champ.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:52.140
That was a great spar.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.520
It helped me get in the swing of things.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.760
Wait, wait!

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.150
I'm still fine!

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.370
Date-san!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.480
<i>He beat me.</i>

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:07.260
<i>I'm not under any weight control and in my best condition...</i>

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:08.700
<i>And he just brushed me off.</i>

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.660
<i>He would've definitely knocked me down.</i>

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:14.510
<i>Miyata-kun was beaten so easily.</i>

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:16.580
<i>I can't believe it!</i>

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:19.670
So strong...

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:23.810
Date-san's like a different person from when he fought me.

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:26.430
At that rate, he'd be able to beat the world champion too!

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.160
B-But...

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.440
the world champion is strong too.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.180
But Date-san was also...

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.740
I don't know!

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.390
You were watching, weren't you?

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.790
U-Um...

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:42.440
Well, that is...

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:44.440
Did you see?

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:50.520
You caught me at a bad time.

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:53.600
N-No, it was an incredible spar!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.520
More like I caught you at a good time.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.730
You've got to be kidding.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:19:59.600
Honestly,

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.700
he would've knocked me down if we had kept at it.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.750
My head's still spinning.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.270
Me too!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.960
I was almost knocked down by the world champion!

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:12.740
We're the same!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.330
That kind of pisses me off.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.480
But still,

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.560
the Japanese Champion and the Pacific Champion.

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:23.480
We've both been able to distinguish ourselves a little bit, but we've still got a long way to go.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.000
We really learned something.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:28.650
Yeah...

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:30.990
learned it the hard way.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.530
The world's a big place.
